# kk: Merge timestamp resolves at the end of the command buffer
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46472 state=opened
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Merge timestamp resolves at the end of the command buffer

Each resolveCounterHeap runs as a separate encoder inside the command buffer and the GPU idles around it. KosmicKrisp resolved after every encoder that wrote a timestamp, so a command buffer paid one idle gap per such encoder.

This keeps pending resolves until vkEndCommandBuffer, or until a query reset or copy needs them, then sorts them and merges runs of consecutive heap entries with contiguous reports into one resolve. Resetting or freeing a command buffer that is still recording drops its pending resolves without encoding them, so a query pool destroyed in the meantime is never touched.

In Enshrouded (through Wine) the average frame rate goes from 30.4 to 31.9 FPS (+4.7% over three paired runs); the slowest frames did not improve in two of the three pairs.

Testing (Apple M5 Pro, macOS 27.2): every timestamp case in the Vulkan mustpass (1,102 cases, 398 supported, all pass, also with Metal API validation, no messages) and a 79,312 case list, with no regressions against main.
